; Cranelisp — modules and imports
; The standard library is modules. You pull names in on demand.

; /imports shows what is currently in scope. At the start that is just the
; prelude (operators, the common types, Some/None) plus special forms:

/imports

; The collection verbs are NOT bare — they live in collections.vec. Import
; the ones you want by name; the REPL confirms each:

(import [collections.vec [count get assoc]])
/imports

; An imported name reports its fully-qualified origin when you type it:

count
/info count

; Now use them unqualified:

(count (vec 10 20 30))
(get (vec 10 20 30) 1)
(assoc (vec 10 20 30) 0 99)

; List operations live in collections.list — first and rest return Option:

(import [collections.list [first rest]])
(first (list 1 2 3))
(rest (list 1 2 3))

; A name you have not imported is simply unbound — the REPL tells you what
; it knows, it does not guess. Type one and see:

vec-reverse

; Import it from its module and it resolves:

(import [collections.vec [vec-reverse]])
(vec-reverse (vec 1 2 3))

; This is how the Sudoku exemplar is built: grid, solver, html, and form
; are four modules, each importing only what it needs from the others and
; from the prelude. `cranelisp exemplar/user.cl` wires them together.
